# gpu-lanes.env — THE source of truth for which card does what on billie.
#
# Nothing else may encode a card choice. Services pin the UUID below through
# `bin/gpu-lanes apply`; tools read this file (or the VF_* env vars it exports)
# and never use a numeric index. Why: three numbering schemes disagree here and
# every one of them has silently meant a different card at some point.
#
#   nvidia-smi order : 0 = 750 Ti   1 = V100 A (02:00)   2 = V100 B (03:00)
#   CUDA order       : 0 = V100 A   1 = V100 B           2 = 750 Ti
#   --cuda-device N  : an ordinal INTO CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES, so it changes
#                      meaning the moment that list changes (this is what broke)
#
# Roles (Dylan, 2026-11-06):
#   A = media in   : stills (:8189), audio + music, vision, voice (TTS/STT)
#   B = heavy out  : video + 3D (:8190), the lazy writer LLM
#   display        : GTX 750 Ti — screen + h264_nvenc only. Never a model.

# --- Tesla V100-PCIE-32GB, PCI 0000:02:00.0 — lane A ---------------------------
# PCI 2 -> port 8189 (stills) + audio/music + vision + voice
GPU_A_PCI=0000:02:00.0
GPU_A_UUID=GPU-4b080f71-df07-0179-37d9-ddbb3cc41e24
GPU_A_LABEL="V100 A · stills + audio/music + vision + voice"

# --- Tesla V100-PCIE-32GB, PCI 0000:03:00.0 — lane B ---------------------------
# PCI 3 -> port 8190 (video + 3D) + the lazy writer
GPU_B_PCI=0000:03:00.0
GPU_B_UUID=GPU-a67b1ea5-e15f-37ae-82d6-4be3ed821109
GPU_B_LABEL="V100 B · video + 3D + writer"

# --- GTX 750 Ti, PCI 01:00.0 — display only -----------------------------------
GPU_DISPLAY_PCI=0000:01:00.0
GPU_DISPLAY_UUID=GPU-c5b7fb20-f2ff-8ecc-8799-a8291f5b8027

# Ports (the ports ARE the lane interface; a client picks a lane by port)
COMFY_VIDEO_PORT=8190     # comfyui-b.service   -> lane B (PCI 3)
COMFY_STILLS_PORT=8189    # comfyui.service     -> lane A (PCI 2)
VISION_PORT=8200          # vision-vl.service   -> lane A
WRITER_PORT=8101          # qwen14-lazy gateway -> llama-qwen14 on lane B
TTS_PORT=3200             # voice-tts.service   -> lane A
STT_PORT=3201             # voice-stt.service   -> lane A
